ing features into types/interfaces, implementation, and tests. The existing open issues cover the main work for pkg/testutils and cmd/ts, but I need to check if they're properly decomposed according to this principle or if there's a gap in the task breakdown that should be proposed instead. existing issues:\n- `dtl`: \"Implement pkg/testutils differential testing harness (prd001 R1-R5)\" - this seems to be the full implementation\n- `imv`: \"Implement cmd/ts timestamp utility (prd004-ts R1-R8)\" - this seems to be the full implementation\n\nBut P2 says to split implementation and tests. However, these already exist as open issues with a certain scope. I shouldn't duplicate them.\n\nWait, let me re-read more carefully. The constraint says:\n- \"Do NOT exceed 1 tasks.\"\n- \"Do NOT duplicate existing issues.\"\n\nSo I need to propose exactly 1 task that is NOT duplicating the existing open issues.\n\nLooking at what's needed for rel01.0:\n1. pkg/testutils implementation (already covered by open issue `dtl`)\n2. cmd/ts implementation (already covered by open issue `imv`)\n\nWhat might be missing? The existing issues cover R1-R5 for pkg/testutils and R1-R8 for cmd/ts, but prd004-ts R9 specifically requires differential tests using the TimestampNormalizer, which isn't explicitly covered by the current scope of `imv`.\n\nSo the missing task would be implementing differential tests for cmd/ts that use the TimestampNormalizer - this depends on both pkg/testutils and cmd/ts being completed first, but it's a distinct task that fills the gap. from both existing issues\n- Maps to rel01.0-uc001-ts \n- Anchored to prd004-ts R9\n- Depends on both existing issues being complete\n\nThis seems like the right thing to propose.\n\nLet me now structure the task:\n\n**Task: Implement differential tests for cmd/ts (prd004-ts R9)**\n\nThis task would:\n- Create `cmd/ts/ts_test.go` with differential tests using pkg/testutils\n- Use TimestampNormalizer for normalizing output\n- Cover all test cases from test-rel01.0\n\nActually wait, I need to reconsider. The task says to propose 1 task (max), and the existing issues already open are:\n1. pkg/testutils implementation\n2. cmd/ts implementation (R1-R8)\n\nThese open issues need to be completed first before we can write tests. But I can still propose the test task to be done after the implementation issues are done.\n\nSo I'll write up the differential test task for `cmd/ts` that covers prd004-ts R9 and test-rel01.0, creating the test file with requirements for the RunDiffTests structure using TimestampNormalizer, covering the three default format test cases, custom strftime and subsecond extensions, and both elapsed and incremental modes.\n\nI'm also thinking about the design decisions here: using pkg/testutils RunDiffTests per prd001 R4, applying TimestampNormalizer to all tests with wall-clock timestamps per prd004-ts R9.1, and determining the test binary paths. Given the constraint of 150-250 lines per task, a test file with 12 test cases should fit comfortably within that range.\n\nFor acceptance criteria, I need to ensure go test ./cmd/ts/... passes all 12 test cases, each test is a named subtest using t.Run, tests with wall-clock output apply TimestampNormalizer before comparison, the empty stdin test produces no output and exits 0, the invalid flag test verifies non-zero exit with usage message in stderr, and cmd/ts_test.go compiles cleanly under golangci-lint.\n\nI should reference the product requirements in prd004-ts.yaml for R1-R9 requirements, check test-suites/test-rel01.0.yaml for all 12 test cases, and look at prd001-testutils.yaml for the RunDiffTests API and TimestampNormalizer. The actual implementation files like pkg/testutils/difftest.go don't exist yet on the working branch, so I'll need to rely on the PRD specifications instead. This test task depends on both pkg/testutils and cmd/ts being implemented first, which are open issues, but that's fine since there's a clear dependency ordering.\n\nSince I'm only proposing one task and the dependencies reference other tasks in the current batch by index, I'll set dependency to -1 even though this logically depends on those other open issues that are already tracked separately.\n\nBut I'm realizing the real constraint: the stitch agent only sees the task description and project rules, so if I propose a test task that depends on pkg/testutils and cmd/ts, the description needs to make those dependencies explicit enough for the agent to understand what's required before starting work. Looking at the existing issue for cmd/ts, it covers the core implementation (R1-R8), so what's missing is the actual Go test code that validates those implementations against the test cases defined in the spec. That's the natural next task to propose. This covers R1-R8. But prd004-ts also has R9 (differential testing). The issue title explicitly says R1-R8, excluding R9. So R9 (the test implementation) is indeed a separate task.\n\nMy proposed task:\n\n**Title**: Implement cmd/ts differential tests (prd004-ts R9)\n\nThis seems right. Let me write it up properly.\n\nFor the required_reading, I need to include:\n- prd004-ts.yaml (for R9 requirements and the ts behavior)\n- test-rel01.0.yaml (for the 12 test cases to implement)\n- prd001-testutils.yaml (for RunDiffTests API, TimestampNormalizer)\n\nFor files:\n- cmd/ts/ts_test.go (create)\n\nFor requirements, I'm targeting 5-8 per P9. I need to set up the test harness using the RunDiffTests framework, then cover the main test scenarios: default format handling with various stdin patterns, custom strftime formats with subsecond extensions, and the different timestamp modes like elapsed-since-start and incremental. Now I'm laying out the design decisions: applying TimestampNormalizer to all wall-clock timestamp tests, structuring each test as a named subtest, using the reference `ts` binary from moreutils alongside the Go binary in bin/, and ensuring all tests run with LC_ALL=C and a fixed timezone. The acceptance criteria requires all 12 test cases to pass. I'm verifying the scope looks reasonable—8 requirements, 5 acceptance criteria, and 4 design decisions all fall within the expected ranges, and the test file should be around 180-240 lines across 12 test cases. Now I'm drafting the final YAML specification for this task. I need to cover additional test cases for custom strftime formats with subsecond precision, elapsed-since-start and incremental modes, and monotonic clock mode, all mapped to their corresponding requirements in the product spec. I'm looking at the design decisions for how to structure the test implementation. I need to apply the TimestampNormalizer to wall-clock timestamp tests while keeping deterministic tests without it, organize each test case as a named subtest matching the original test names, and figure out how to locate the Go binary relative to the module. Generating acceptance criteria... The task depends on pkg/testutils and cmd/ts being implemented first, but since the stitch agent writes code rather than runs it, the tests would compile and execute later once those dependencies are ready. The orchestrator should handle sequencing these tasks appropriately given the dependency chain. I'll finalize the task description now, making sure to note that pkg/testutils is available via the PRD even if the implementation isn't complete yet, and letting the orchestrator handle the dependency sequencing between this task and the earlier dtl issue.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":74086,"cache_read_input_tokens":15559,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":74086},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b749544a-92bc-48c8-9193-512be986c608","uuid":"3932c5f2-b732-43e7-aaf1-78af1169e910"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01NKHZXREUZCZSNw3EpZ392k","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Step 2: Project State Summary\n\n**Problem**: Classic Unix utilities lack formal specifications. This project derives specs from C source code, generates Go implementations via AI orchestration, and verifies parity with GNU reference binaries through differential testing.\n\n**Architecture**: Four-stage pipeline (extract → specify → synthesize → verify). Key components: `cmd/` (one package per utility), `pkg/testutils/` (differential harness), `pkg/sys/` (syscall abstractions), `pkg/format/` (output formatting), `magefiles/` (Mage build targets). Human operator owns specs; mage-claude-orchestrator owns code generation.\n\n**Current State**: All generated code lives at generation-merged tags (not on the working branch). Specs are complete for: pkg/testutils, pkg/sys, pkg/format, cmd/ts, cmd/wc, cmd/cat, cmd/sponge, cmd/ls (PRDs only), cmd/du (PRD only).\n\n**Current Release**: `rel01.0` is `in_progress`. Use case `rel01.0-uc001-ts` is `in_progress`.\n\n## Step 3: Priority Analysis\n\nEarliest incomplete release: **rel01.0** (ts timestamp utility).\n\nExisting open issues in the tracker:\n- `dtl`: Implement pkg/testutils (prd001 R1-R5) — covers harness implementation\n- `imv`: Implement cmd/ts (prd004-ts R1-R8) — covers utility implementation, explicitly excludes R9\n\n**Gap**: prd004-ts R9 (differential tests for cmd/ts) is not covered by any open issue. Per P2, implementation and tests must be separate tasks. The test file `cmd/ts/ts_test.go` implementing the 12 test cases from test-rel01.0 is the missing deliverable for rel01.0 to be verifiable.\n\n## Step 4: Proposed Task\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"Implement cmd/ts differential tests (prd004-ts R9)\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/product-requirements/prd004-ts.yaml (R9 requirements for differential testing, test coverage list)\n      - docs/specs/test-suites/test-rel01.0.yaml (all 12 test cases to implement as Go subtests)\n      - docs/specs/product-requirements/prd001-testutils.yaml (RunDiffTests API, TimestampNormalizer contract, DiffTest struct fields)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/ts/ts_test.go\n        action: create\n        note: Differential tests for cmd/ts using pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests and TimestampNormalizer\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Implement a TestTs function that calls pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests with the Go binary\n          (bin/ts, located relative to module root) and the reference binary (ts on PATH from\n          moreutils) per prd004-ts R9.1 and prd001-testutils R4; skip the test suite if either\n          binary is absent\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Cover default format mode: three-line stdin, empty stdin producing no output with\n          exit 0, and partial last line with no trailing newline per test-rel01.0 test cases\n          default_format_three_lines, default_format_empty_stdin, default_format_partial_last_line\n          and prd004-ts R1\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Cover custom strftime format string and subsecond %.S extension (seconds with\n          microsecond suffix) per test-rel01.0 test cases custom_strftime_format and\n          subsecond_format_dotS and prd004-ts R2\"\n      - id: R4\n        text: \"Cover -s elapsed-since-start mode and -i incremental mode per test-rel01.0 test\n          cases elapsed_since_start_mode and incremental_mode and prd004-ts R3 and R4\"\n      - id: R5\n        text: \"Cover -m monotonic clock mode per test-rel01.0 test case monotonic_clock_mode and\n          prd004-ts R5\"\n      - id: R6\n        text: \"Cover -r relative mode: syslog-format timestamp converted to relative age, and\n          line with no recognizable timestamp passed through unchanged per test-rel01.0 test cases\n          relative_mode_syslog_timestamp and relative_mode_no_timestamp_passthrough and\n          prd004-ts R6\"\n      - id: R7\n        text: \"Cover error cases: -i and -s mutual exclusion (non-zero exit, stderr contains\n          usage), and unrecognized flag -z (non-zero exit, stderr contains usage) per\n          test-rel01.0 test cases incremental_and_elapsed_mutually_exclusive and invalid_flag\n          and prd004-ts R7\"\n      - id: R8\n        text: \"Cover TZ environment variable: DiffTest.Env set to TZ=UTC causes timestamps in UTC\n          per test-rel01.0 test case tz_environment_respected and prd004-ts R8; apply\n          TimestampNormalizer to all wall-clock timestamp tests per prd004-ts R9.1\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"Apply TimestampNormalizer from pkg/testutils to all DiffTest cases whose output\n          contains wall-clock timestamps (default format, custom format, subsecond, -m mode,\n          -r syslog, TZ=UTC test); set Normalize to nil for deterministic-output tests (empty\n          stdin, error exits, -r passthrough) per prd004-ts R9.1\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"Each DiffTest is executed as a named subtest using t.Run with the test case name\n          from test-rel01.0 (e.g., \\\"default_format_three_lines\\\") per prd001-testutils R3.6\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"All DiffTest.Env slices include LC_ALL=C and TZ=America/New_York unless a test\n          case explicitly overrides TZ (tz_environment_respected sets TZ=UTC); this matches the\n          preconditions in test-rel01.0\"\n      - id: D4\n        text: \"Use TestMain to build bin/ts via go build before the test suite runs, or skip all\n          tests with t.Skip if the binary is not present; do not hard-code an absolute path for\n          the reference binary -- use exec.LookPath(\\\"ts\\\") and skip if not found\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"All 12 test cases from test-rel01.0 are implemented as named t.Run subtests in\n          cmd/ts/ts_test.go\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"go test ./cmd/ts/... passes when bin/ts and the reference binary ts are both\n          available on the test host with moreutils installed\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"Tests that produce wall-clock timestamps apply TimestampNormalizer before\n          comparison; tests with deterministic output (empty stdin, error exits, -r passthrough)\n          use nil Normalize\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"Error-case tests (mutual exclusion, invalid flag) assert non-zero exit code and\n          that stderr contains the substring \\\"usage\\\"\"\n      - id: AC5\n        text: \"cmd/ts/ts_test.go compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint\"\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":74086,"cache_read_input_tokens":15559,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":74086},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b749544a-92bc-48c8-9193-512be986c608","uuid":"bbcfe46f-2a79-40dd-aa91-e8e37c407612"}
